  "HDDS-5965": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-5965",
    "issue_type": "New Feature",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Recon should be able to distinguish between containers that have no replicas and those have all replicas as UNHEALTHY.",
    "description": "The ContainerHealthTask in Recon currently classifies a container whose 3 replicas are UNHEALTHY as 'MISSING'.  Although the 3 UNHEALTHY replica state could also be potentially bad, Recon should be able to distinguish between the two.\r\n\r\nThe above case can merely be classified as UNDER REPLICATED, with the metadata from Recon DB carrying the actual vs desired replica count for further analysis.",
    "commits": [
