  "HDDS-6053": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-6053",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Implemented",
    "title": "Fix too short container scrubber data scan interval.",
    "description": "I've found that the datanode container data scrubber defaults to have an scan interval if 1minute:\r\n{code:java}\r\n// ContainerScrubberConfiguration.java\r\n@Config(key = \"data.scan.interval\",\r\n    type = ConfigType.TIME,\r\n    defaultValue = \"1m\", \r\n...{code}\r\nIt is too short since data scan is a heavy read load which may make normal IO slow,\r\n\r\nso a longer interval should be used as default, for example 1d.\r\n\r\n ",
